=== ANSWER A ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: git ls-files | wc -l && git ls-files | sed -n 's/.*\.\([^./]*\)$/\1/p' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -40
 - Bash: git ls-files -z | while IFS= read -r -d '' f; do
  case "$f" in *.*) ext="${f##*.}";; *) ext="(no ext)";; esac
  git blame --line-porcelain -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | sed -n 's/^author //p' | sed "s/^/$ext\t/"
done | sort | uniq -c | sort -k2,2 -k1,1rn | awk '{c=$1; $1=""; print c"\t"substr($0,2)}' > /tmp/blame_ext.txt; cat /tmp/blame_ext.txt | column -t -s$'\t' | head -100
 - Bash: git log -1 --format='%an <%ae>' 62628c0 && git log -1 --format='%an' b2005d9 && git ls-files '*.js' | xargs -I{} git blame --line-porcelain -- {} | grep -c '^author Fiona' ; git ls-files '*.js' | xargs -n1 git blame --line-porcelain -- | sed -n 's/^author //p' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -3; echo ---; git ls-files '*.js' | xargs -I{} sh -c 'wc -l < "{}"' | paste -sd+ | bc
 - Bash: git ls-files '*.js' | xargs -n1 git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0 --line-porcelain -- | sed -n 's/^author //p' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -4
FINAL ANSWER:
Surviving-line owners per file type, from `git blame` on HEAD (18 tracked files):

| Ext | Files | Top owner (surviving lines) | Runner-up |
|---|---|---|---|
| `js` | 7 | **Fiona Formatter**, 1016 (see note) | Troy Goode, 139 |
| `yml` | 6 | **Douglas Christopher Wilson**, 117 | Íñigo Marquínez Prado, 94 |
| `md` | 2 | **Troy Goode**, 104 | Jon Church, 72 |
| `json` | 1 | **Douglas Christopher Wilson**, 20 | Troy Goode, 12 |
| `gitignore` | 1 | **Douglas Christopher Wilson**, 4 | Troy Goode, 1 |
| no extension | 1 | **Douglas Christopher Wilson**, 17 | Troy Goode, 5 |

Note on `js`: Fiona Formatter's 1016 lines come from commit `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes"), which rewrote almost every line. Ignoring that commit with `git blame --ignore-rev`, the `js` ranking becomes **Troy Goode 520**, **Douglas Christopher Wilson 339**, Fiona Formatter 237, Alejandro Caravaca Puchades 26. Under that view, Troy Goode is the top `js` owner.

Method: plain `git blame --line-porcelain` per tracked file, grouped by extension, no `-M`/`-C`/`-w`. Line counts are blame attributions, not authorship quality.

=== ANSWER B ===
