 - Bash: [ -f "<home>/claude-kredi-runs/2026-10-23/r11/ours-src/bin/<tool>" ] && node "<home>/claude-kredi-runs/2026-10-23/r11/ours-src/bin/<tool>" --group-by ext --merge-identities
 - Bash: node "<home>/claude-kredi-runs/2026-10-23/r11/ours-src/bin/<tool>" --group-by ext 2>&1 | head -60
FINAL ANSWER:
**Who owns the most surviving lines, per file extension** (ref `HEAD`, 1,662 of 1,672 lines attributed; 1,662 non-blank lines, 1,995 with blank lines)

| Extension | Top owner (merged) | Lines | Share | Bus factor (50%) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `.js` (1,032 lines) | Troy Goode (2 addresses) | 564 | 54.7% | 1: Troy alone |
| `.yml` (314 lines) | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 101 | 32.2% | 2: Douglas + Íñigo Marquínez Prado (57.6%) |
| `.md` (253 lines) | Troy Goode | 71 | 28.1% | 2: Troy + Jon Church (51.4%) |
| `.json` (40 lines) | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 | 50.0% | 1: Douglas alone |
| no extension (23 lines) | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 21 | 91.3% | 1: Douglas alone |

**Troy Goode, `.js`.** Merged, 564 lines (54.7%). Unmerged: `<email redacted>` 520 (50.4%) and `troy@laptop.example` 44 (4.3%). The merge is a guess from the same name, not confirmed. The `.md` figure is the same either way, because all 71 lines sit under the gmail address. Troy's share falls below half only in the unmerged view. Bus factor is 1 in both views.

**Other rows:**
- `.js`: Douglas Christopher Wilson 362 (35.1%), alex94puchades 30 (2.9%), then 11 more authors below 2%.
- `.yml`: Íñigo Marquínez Prado 80 (25.5%), Sebastian Beltran 53 (16.9%), Ulises Gascón 41 (13.1%), Ignacio Mangas 38 (12.1%), Carlos Serrano 1 (0.3%).
- `.md`: Jon Church 59 (23.3%), Douglas 47 (18.6%), Linus Unnebäck 26 (10.3%), Ollie Buck 14 (5.5%), Efe 6 (2.4%), plus 14 more authors.
- `.json`: Troy 12 (30.0%), Sebastian Beltran 4 (10.0%), then 1-line holders.
- No extension (23 lines): Douglas 21 (91.3%), Troy 2 (8.7%).

No `.js`, `.yml`, `.md` or `.json` row has an owner holding everything. Only the extensionless files have one owner over half.

**Identity note.** The tool also reports `alex94puchades` (`<email redacted>`, 30 `.js` lines) and `Alejandro Caravaca Puchades` as one address under two names. Its `.js` table still shows `alex94puchades` as a separate row, so I am not sure the merge applies there. I did not write any `.mailmap` file, since you asked a question, not for a fix.

**Left out:**
- `dependabot[bot]`: 10 lines, 11 commits, excluded as a bot.
- Commit `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes", Fiona Formatter, 2026-04-12): set aside as a whitespace/quote-only change, so the `.js` figures leave it out. Without that correction, overall Troy is 33.3% and Douglas 22.6%. The tool gives no per-extension figures for that view.
- Mechanical-rewrite check: 136 commits examined, 1 set aside (`62628c0`). Five more look mechanical and are kept in the counts: `739dc11` (docs: reformat license, Douglas, 17 lines), `fcd2b56` (ESLint switch, Troy, 11 lines), `00d6eec` (Douglas, 9 lines), `344ce1e` (Douglas, 1 line), `9c2b59d` (Douglas, 1 line). I did not inspect these with `git show --stat`, so I have not confirmed they are mechanical.

**Method.** Blame was run with `git blame -w -M -C` and `--ignore-rev 62628c0`. The tool printed no copy-detection note, so no share moved by more than 2 points under copy detection. Bus factor counts lines: the fewest authors whose surviving lines reach 50% of the lines counted. Per-extension results cover the whole repository (18 of 18 files, no sampling). Shares are of non-blank lines. Surviving lines measure survivorship, not quality, and they do not show review or design work.

=== ANSWER C ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: git ls-files | wc -l && git ls-files | sed -n 's/.*\.\([^./]*\)$/\1/p' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -30
 - Bash: for f in $(git ls-files); do case "$f" in *.*) ext="${f##*.}";; *) ext="(none)";; esac; git blame --line-porcelain -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | sed -n 's/^author //p' | sed "s/^/$ext\t/"; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -k2,2 -k1,1rn | awk '{c=$1; $1=""; print c"\t"$0}'
 - Bash: git ls-files | grep -v '\.' ; echo ---; git show -s --format='%H %an %s' 62628c0; echo ---; for f in $(git ls-files | grep '\.js$'); do git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0 --line-porcelain -- "$f" 2>/dev/null | sed -n 's/^author //p'; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -8
FINAL ANSWER:
Per extension, by surviving lines from `git blame` on HEAD (18 tracked files):

| Extension | Top owner | Lines | Share of ext | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `.js` (1,202) | Fiona Formatter | 1,016 | 85% | Almost all from one reformat commit (`62628c0`, "style: reformat js…"). Ignoring that commit with `--ignore-rev`, Troy Goode leads with 520 lines, then Douglas Christopher Wilson with 339. |
| `.md` (341) | Troy Goode | 104 | 30% | Jon Church (72) and Douglas Christopher Wilson (67) are next. |
| `.yml` (383) | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 117 | 31% | Íñigo Marquínez Prado is close (94). |
| `.json` (43) | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 | 47% | Troy Goode has 12. |
| `.gitignore` (5) | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 4 | 80% | |
| no extension (`LICENSE`, 22) | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 17 | 77% | Troy Goode has 5. |

The `.js` result depends on how you count. Raw blame credits the formatter commit's author. Excluding that commit, Troy Goode owns the most surviving JS lines.
